  "assembly_dimensions": "../../parts/next-pairs/geometry.json",
  "methods": {
    "paths": "Read each identified part from the final native archive, remove its plate placement and expand each outer road by half its commanded width. Positive ramp gap is horizontal air from the receiver guide to the inside cover face. Positive retaining-shoulder overlap means the registered faces occupy common radial space.",
    "square_registration": "At both feet on all 46 interior cover courses, invert the free spring camber and local rotation. Measure the crest 0.03 mm inside the deposited face. At the −4.5, 0 and +4.5 mm axial stations align the two feet to the measured receiver roof, compare the 45° shoulders at ordinary course midheight, and sample the crown at 0.01 mm spacing. The square_feet ramp values use this registration.",
    "shoulder_loaded_registration": "Starting with the same measured contours, solve the additional signed outward spring displacement of each tip until the largest mid-course retaining-shoulder overlap just clears. At every trial displacement the lowest rotated foot meets the printed 3.56 mm roof. The beam bends about its neutral axis and the saddle stays rigid. This calculation estimates how shoulder tension could open the approach gap. It does not measure the deflected shape, pressure or force of the printed plastic.",
    "ramp_sampling": "For each of three axial stations on both hooks, intersect the cover envelope near both edges and at the midpoint of every receiver course from 0.24 to 6.16 mm behind the toe. The measured inward step is the reduction in the fixed receiver radius from one emitted 0.24 mm course to the next on this slope. Three additional radial-gap measurements are at 0.55, 3.20 and 5.85 mm from the deposited roof. The endpoint bevels, toolpath corner rounding and bead compression lie outside this interior comparison."
  },
